#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""board brief: ONE message per cluster per day, built on `board health`.

The brief says what the reader must DO. Every line of the main body starts with a verb and
names what to act on. A line that needs no action from the reader goes to the one Handled
line, to the weekly Details, or is dropped. Agent faults (a sync error, an incident the agent
already works) are never a decision. Instant alerts stay on their own rails; the brief never
replaces them.

Message order, separated by a blank line only where a heading starts:

  Your call (N)         `### 🙋 Your call (N)`, one bullet per item, most urgent first: an operator
                        `--line` that opens with 👉 and holds ` by <Day D Mon>` (marker dropped),
                        nearest date first; incident rows the --incidents hook marks `needs_you`,
                        as `<action> <id>: <label> (<facts>)` when the row carries an `action`
                        (<= 40 chars), else `<id> <label>: <question>` with the closing question
                        in bold, "Triage or map" before "Close"; the hook's explicit `decisions`;
                        any other 👉 line; hub/mirror drift (`ID hub/mirror drift: ... **Ship or
                        reopen?**`); a board past its triage threshold, as `Triage N <board> cards
                        waiting Nd: "<title>", "<title>"` (two titles at most, 40 chars each, the
                        `untrusted ` marker dropped), longest wait first; a linked Hermes profile
                        whose kit skills are stale (`board hermes check`). Three lines show, the
                        rest is one `+N more` line, so the cap drops the least urgent; the count
                        in the head is the whole list. With none and no error, `### ✅ Nothing needs you today` stands
                        alone.
  Handled               ONE line, `🤖 Handled: a · b · c`, directly under the block: the operator
                        `--line` fragments that open with 🤖 (marker dropped), `N incident(s) with
                        chonky` for open incidents that are not decisions, then the sync and bots
                        state: `sync and bots clean`, or `❌ sync errors N`, `⚠️ sync warnings N`,
                        `❌ feed unreadable`, `❌ feed faults N`.
  Details               a follow-up field, only on Mondays (Vietnam time) or under --show-boards:
                        the board lines (hub, board, fault, extra), the operator's other --line
                        lines, the hook's `details`, the bot counts (the hook's and the archived
                        count), then any error lines. On any other day it is dropped unless an
                        error exists, and then it holds the error lines only.

`severity` is `warn` only when Your call is not empty or an error exists (a sync error or
warning, an unreadable feed, a hook fault); else `info`. `footer_tail` in the payload is true
only on a Details day, for the poster to keep or drop its footer tail text.

Ids are links, never plain text: a board row id is a masked link to its line in the GitHub
copy of the board (`[ID-538](<https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/blob/BRANCH/FILE?plain=1#L183>)`,
read from the repo's origin remote and `git grep` on the origin ref), a hook row or decision
with a `url` is a masked link to it. Every link has its URL in angle brackets, so Discord shows
no preview. An id with no URL (the repo is not on GitHub, the hook gave none) is inline code.
A host after `@` is inline code. A hook URL must be https and free of markup characters.

Incident hook (--incidents C=CMD): CMD prints one JSON object on stdout, so any
operator's incident source fits. Every key is optional:

  {"open":    [{"id","label","host","url","age","firing":bool,"needs_you":bool,"question","action"}],
   "decisions": [{"id","url","question"}],  explicit decision lines
   "bots":    {"auto-resolved": 3},      counts of what bots did, shown in the weekly Details
   "faults":  ["line", ...],             fault lines: an error, shown in Details
   "details": ["line", ...]}             extra lines for the weekly Details

`action` is an imperative of 40 chars or fewer ("Close", "Triage or map"). With it a needs_you
row reads `• <action> <id>: <label> (<facts>)`, the facts being the question's `fired Nx, quiet Nd`
text without its trailing hint or question; without it the row reads as `<id> <label>: <question>`.

A hook that fails, or prints something that is not that object, becomes a fault
line: the brief never claims "all clear" over an unreadable feed. Under --dry-run
and --no-state the hook runs with BOARD_BRIEF_READ_ONLY=1 in its environment and
must write nothing (no alert, no heartbeat).

The payload (one JSON line per cluster, stdout under --dry-run), handed to
--poster on stdin; exit 0 means the main message was delivered:
  {kind: "brief", cluster, rail, key, severity: info|warn (warn: Your call is not empty or an
   error exists; the poster maps it to the card mark), title, date,
   period_days: 1, next_due, attention: bool (a decision item exists),
   footer_tail: bool (a Details day: keep the rail's footer tail text),
   fields: [{name, value}]  the main message, one line per field
   details: [line, ...]     the follow-up message, absent when empty
   carried_error?, data: {...}}
The poster delivers the details as a second message (a thread reply where the
rail supports one). A failed details post never fails the main post.

Flags (the source flags are `board health run`'s: --registry --cluster-map
--state-file --health-state-file --stale-days --sync-stale-hours --kanban --line
--hub --board --triage-open --triage-days):
  --config F            flags from a JSON file, see `board health run`; the
                        section name is `brief`
  --incidents C=CMD     incident hook for cluster C (repeatable)
  --decisions-only C    cluster C posts only when a decision item exists, and the
                        message is the decision lines alone
  --every-days N        cadence (default 1); a failed post is not stamped, so it
                        stays due and rides `carried_error`
  --boards-every-days N accepted and ignored (the boards ride the Monday Details now)
  --show-boards         treat the day as a Details day (a preview)
  --main-chars N        budget for the main message (default 1250, under the poster's 1380
                        cap with its footer): over it, the Your call lines past the first
                        collapse into the `+N more` line
  --poster CMD          delivers one payload on stdin
  --cluster C           only this cluster
  --force               ignore the cadence
  --dry-run             print payloads, post nothing, write nothing
  --no-state            post for real but write no stamp or baseline (a live test)
  --now EPOCH           pin the clock (tests)

State lives in the health state file under `brief`, beside the sweep's records.
stderr: `brief: ...` log lines. Exit 0 on a normal run; only a usage error is nonzero.
"""

import argparse
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone
from pathlib import Path

HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent


sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))
import sweep_modules  # noqa: E402

H = sweep_modules.load("board-health")
HM = sweep_modules.load("board-hermes")
DAY = H.DAY
ORIGIN_ID_RE = re.compile(r"^origin:\s*([^\s:]+):(\S+)", re.M)
TERMINAL_ROW = ("shipped", "dropped", "done", "closed")
MAX_DECISIONS = 3
HAND = "👉"
ROBOT = "🤖"
AGENT = "chonky"
VN_TZ = timezone(timedelta(hours=7))


def log(msg):
    print(f"brief: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)


# --- the incident hook ---------------------------------------------------------

def _text(value, cap=200):
    """One printable line from a hook value. Secrets are masked (webhook URLs, secret
    references, long hex or base64 runs); a name like `some_rule-crit` is kept whole.
    Markup characters are dropped so a hook value cannot forge a link or a code span."""
    if value is None:
        return ""
    text = "".join(c if c.isprintable() else " " for c in str(value))
    text = re.sub(r"[`<>\[\]*]", "", text)
    text = re.sub(r"https://discord(app)?\.com/api/webhooks/\S+", "[webhook-redacted]", text)
    text = re.sub(r"op://\S+", "[ref-redacted]", text)
    text = re.sub(r"\b[0-9a-fA-F]{32,}\b|\b[A-Za-z0-9+/=]{40,}\b", "[redacted]", text)
    return re.sub(r"\s+", " ", text).strip()[:cap]


URL_RE = re.compile(r"^https://[^\s<>()\[\]`]{1,300}$")


def _url(value):
    """A hook URL: https only, no markup characters, no webhook; else empty."""
    v = str(value or "").strip()
    return v if URL_RE.match(v) and "/api/webhooks/" not in v else ""


def link(text, url):
    """A masked link with the preview suppressed, or the text in inline code when there is no URL."""
    return f"[{text}](<{url}>)" if url else f"`{text}`"


def bold_question(text):
    """The closing question of a decision line in bold: `... Ship or reopen?` becomes `... **Ship or reopen?**`."""
    m = re.search(r"([^.!?:]*\?)\s*$", text)
    if not m or not m.group(1).strip():
        return text
    q = m.group(1)
    return text[:m.start(1)] + q[:len(q) - len(q.lstrip())] + "**" + q.strip() + "**"


def code_host(label):
    """`rule @ host` with the host in inline code."""
    return re.sub(r" @ (\S+)", lambda m: f" @ `{m.group(1)}`", label)


def read_incidents(cmd, read_only=False):
    """(data, error): the hook's JSON object, cleaned; error is one short reason.
    Under a preview or a live test the hook runs with BOARD_BRIEF_READ_ONLY=1 and
    must write nothing."""
    env = dict(os.environ, BOARD_BRIEF_READ_ONLY="1") if read_only else None
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(shlex.split(cmd), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=300, env=env)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        return None, H.redact(str(e), 100)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        return None, H.redact(r.stderr or f"exit {r.returncode}", 100)
    try:
        raw = json.loads(r.stdout)
    except ValueError:
        return None, "hook printed no JSON"
    if not isinstance(raw, dict):
        return None, "hook JSON is not an object"
    rows = []
    for o in raw.get("open") or []:
        if isinstance(o, dict):
            rows.append({"id": _text(o.get("id"), 40), "label": _text(o.get("label"), 120),
                         "host": _text(o.get("host"), 60), "url": _url(o.get("url")),
                         "age": _text(o.get("age"), 20), "firing": bool(o.get("firing")),
                         "needs_you": bool(o.get("needs_you")), "question": _text(o.get("question"), 160),
                         "action": _text(o.get("action"), 40)})
    decisions = [{"id": _text(d.get("id"), 40), "url": _url(d.get("url")), "question": _text(d.get("question"), 200)}
                 for d in raw.get("decisions") or [] if isinstance(d, dict) and d.get("question")]
    bots = {str(k)[:40]: v for k, v in (raw.get("bots") or {}).items()
            if isinstance(v, int) and not isinstance(v, bool) and v >= 0} if isinstance(raw.get("bots"), dict) else {}
    return {"open": rows, "decisions": decisions, "bots": bots,
            "faults": [_text(x, 240) for x in raw.get("faults") or [] if x],
            "details": [_text(x, 300) for x in raw.get("details") or [] if x]}, None


def what_of(o):
    """The row's label with its host in inline code (a label that already holds ` @ host` is handled too)."""
    label = code_host(o["label"])
    return label + (f" @ `{o['host']}`" if o["host"] else "")


FACTS_RE = re.compile(r"\b(fired|quiet)\b")
QUESTION_TAIL_RE = re.compile(r"\s*[,.;:]?\s*[^,.;:?]*\?$")


def facts_of(question):
    """The row's question minus a trailing question or hint: `fired 3x · quiet 5d, close?` becomes
    `fired 3x, quiet 5d`; `fired 2x, quiet 1d · some hint` becomes `fired 2x, quiet 1d`. A text with
    no fired or quiet count (`<hint>. Act or close?`) carries no facts."""
    q = QUESTION_TAIL_RE.sub("", question.strip()).strip()
    parts = q.split(" · ")
    if len(parts) > 1 and not FACTS_RE.match(parts[-1]):
        q = " · ".join(parts[:-1])
    return q.replace(" · ", ", ") if FACTS_RE.search(q) else ""


def decision_row(o):
    """A needs_you incident row as a Your call line: its action leads when it has one."""
    ident = link(o["id"], o["url"]) if o["id"] else ""
    if o["action"]:
        facts = facts_of(o["question"])
        lead = f"{o['action']} {ident}".strip() + ":"
        return f"{lead} {what_of(o)}" + (f" ({facts})" if facts else "")
    return f"{ident} {what_of(o)}: {bold_question(o['question'] or 'Act or close?')}".strip()


# --- ids as links ------------------------------------------------------------------------

_repo_info = {}


def repo_info(path):
    """(owner/repo, branch, relative path) for a board file kept on GitHub, else None."""
    if path in _repo_info:
        return _repo_info[path]
    info = None
    p = Path(path)
    top = H.git(p.parent, "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel")
    if p.is_file() and top.returncode == 0 and top.stdout.strip():
        root = top.stdout.strip()
        remote = H.git(root, "remote", "get-url", "origin").stdout.strip()
        m = re.search(r"github\.com[:/]+([^/\s]+)/([^/\s]+?)(?:\.git)?$", remote)
        ref = H.origin_ref(root)
        if m and ref:
            rel = os.path.relpath(os.path.realpath(p), os.path.realpath(root))
            info = (f"{m.group(1)}/{m.group(2)}", ref.split("/", 1)[1], rel, root, ref)
    _repo_info[path] = info
    return info


def row_link(path, rid):
    """A board row id as a masked link to its line in the GitHub copy of the board, else inline code."""
    info = repo_info(path)
    if not info:
        return f"`{rid}`"
    slug, branch, rel, root, ref = info
    r = H.git(root, "grep", "-n", "-E", rf"^\| {re.escape(rid)} \|", ref, "--", rel)
    m = re.search(r":(\d+):", r.stdout.splitlines()[0]) if r.returncode == 0 and r.stdout.strip() else None
    if not m:
        return f"`{rid}`"
    return link(rid, f"https://github.com/{slug}/blob/{branch}/{rel}?plain=1#L{m.group(1)}")


# --- hub/mirror drift ------------------------------------------------------------

def mirror_drift(reader, hub_name, hub_path):
    """Rows whose hub state and mirror card disagree in a way the mirror cannot
    settle by itself: the board says finished and the card is open, or the card is
    done and the board still says live. [{id, board, card, what}], sorted by id."""
    rows = H.hub_rows(hub_path)
    if rows is None:
        return []
    try:
        cards = H.kanban_json(reader, ["--board", hub_name, "list", "--json"])
    except (H.KanbanError, OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return []
    status_of = {}
    for c in cards:
        m = ORIGIN_ID_RE.search(c.get("body") or "")
        if m and m.group(1) == hub_name:
            status_of[m.group(2)] = c.get("status")
    out = []
    for rid, card in sorted(status_of.items()):
        row = rows.get(rid)
        if not row or not row[0]:
            continue
        board = row[0]
        card_open = card not in ("done", "archived")
        board_done = board in TERMINAL_ROW
        if card_open and board_done:
            what = f"board says {board}, the Hermes card is still open"
        elif not card_open and not board_done:
            what = f"the Hermes card is done, the board says {board}"
        else:
            continue
        out.append({"id": rid, "board": board, "card": card, "what": what})
    return out


# --- board lines: count line and triage warning merged ---------------------------------

TRIAGE_FAULT_RE = re.compile(r"^⚠️ (\S+): (\d+) waiting in triage, oldest (\d+)d$")
BOARD_LINE_RE = re.compile(r"^🗂️ (\S+): ")
TITLE_CHARS = 40


UNTRUSTED_RE = re.compile(r"^untrusted\s+", re.I)


def short_title(title):
    """A card title for display: the reader's untrusted-content marker is dropped (the raw title
    stays in the health data, where a model may read it)."""
    t = UNTRUSTED_RE.sub("", _text(title, 200)).replace('"', "'")
    return t if len(t) <= TITLE_CHARS else t[:TITLE_CHARS - 1].rstrip() + "…"


def card_titles(b):
    """` · stale: "A", "B"` for the oldest stale cards (else triage cards), up to three; empty
    when the reader gave no titles."""
    cards = b.get("cards") or []
    stale = [c for c in cards if c.get("stale")]
    label, picked = ("stale", stale) if stale else ("triage", [c for c in cards if c.get("triage")])
    if not picked:
        return ""
    return f" · {label}: " + ", ".join(f'"{short_title(c["title"])}"' for c in picked[:3])


def merged_board_line(slug, b, warn):
    """One line per board: the count, the triage warning folded into the status mix, the stale or
    triage card titles. A board with no warning and nothing stale is a short count line."""
    if not b["open"]:
        text = f"🗂️ {slug}: {b['done']} done, 0 open"
    else:
        mix = b["by_status"]
        if len(mix) == 1 and not (warn and "triage" in mix):
            kinds = next(iter(mix))
        else:
            kinds = ", ".join(f"{k} {v}" + (f" oldest {b['triage_oldest_days']}d" if warn and k == "triage" else "")
                              for k, v in sorted(mix.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]))
        text = f"{'⚠️' if warn else '🗂️'} {slug}: {b['open']} open ({kinds})"
        if warn or b["stale"]:
            titles = card_titles(b)
            text += titles or (f" · {b['stale']} stale" if b["stale"] else "")
    if b["new_since"]:
        text += f" · {b['new_since']} new ticket" + ("" if b["new_since"] == 1 else "s") + " this period"
    return text


MONTHS = ["jan", "feb", "mar", "apr", "may", "jun", "jul", "aug", "sep", "oct", "nov", "dec"]
DEADLINE_RE = re.compile(r" by (?:Mon|Tue|Wed|Thu|Fri|Sat|Sun) (\d{1,2}) (" + "|".join(m.title() for m in MONTHS) + r")\b")


def deadline_of(text, now):
    """The date ordinal of a ` by <Day D Mon>` deadline in a line, else 0. The year is the current
    Vietnam year, or the next when that date is more than two months past."""
    m = DEADLINE_RE.search(text)
    if not m:
        return 0
    today = datetime.fromtimestamp(now, VN_TZ).date()
    try:
        due = today.replace(month=MONTHS.index(m.group(2).lower()) + 1, day=int(m.group(1)))
        if (today - due).days > 60:
            due = due.replace(year=today.year + 1)
    except ValueError:
        return 0
    return due.toordinal()


def triage_action(slug, waiting, oldest_days, board):
    """`Triage N <board> cards waiting Nd: "<title>", "<title>"`: the two oldest triage cards by
    title, none when the reader gave no titles."""
    picked = [c for c in (board or {}).get("cards", []) if c.get("triage")][:2]
    titles = ": " + ", ".join(f'"{short_title(c["title"])}"' for c in picked) if picked else ""
    return f"Triage {waiting} {slug} cards waiting {oldest_days}d{titles}"


def board_lines_of(fields, kanban, listed):
    """The boards block lines from the health fields (hub, board, fault, extra, in order). A listed
    board's count line absorbs its triage warning; a warning for a board with no count line stays
    and gets the titles."""
    warned = {m.group(1) for f in fields if f["name"] == "fault" for m in [TRIAGE_FAULT_RE.match(f["value"])] if m}
    out = []
    for f in fields:
        if f["name"] not in ("hub", "board", "fault", "extra"):
            continue
        v = f["value"]
        m = BOARD_LINE_RE.match(v) if f["name"] == "board" else None
        if m and m.group(1) in kanban:
            out.append(merged_board_line(m.group(1), kanban[m.group(1)], m.group(1) in warned))
            continue
        t = TRIAGE_FAULT_RE.match(v) if f["name"] == "fault" else None
        if t and t.group(1) in listed and t.group(1) in kanban and kanban[t.group(1)]["open"]:
            continue
        out.append(v + (card_titles(kanban[t.group(1)]) if t and t.group(1) in kanban else ""))
    return out


# --- one cluster's brief -----------------------------------------------------------

def compose(cluster, rail, args, rows, health, digest, bstate, now):
    last_run = bstate.get("last_run", {})
    prev_archived = bstate.get("archived", {}).get(cluster, {})
    hview = {k: v for k, v in health.items() if k != "errors"}
    hp, kanban = H.build_payload(cluster, rail, args, rows, hview, digest, last_run, prev_archived, now)

    archived_total = sum((hp["data"].get("archived_since") or {}).values())
    sync_errors = sum(1 for f in hp["fields"] if f["name"] == "attention" and f["value"].startswith("❌"))

    paths = {r["name"]: r["path"] for r in rows}

    # Your call: each line carries its id as a link. Lines sort by urgency (see call_rank); the cap
    # applies after the sort, so the overflow drops the least urgent
    calls = []   # (sort key, text), in collection order
    hub_name = (args.hub_map.get(cluster) or [None])[0]
    reader = (args.kanban_map.get(cluster) or [None])[0]
    drift = []
    if hub_name and reader and hub_name in paths:
        drift = mirror_drift(reader, hub_name, paths[hub_name])
    for d in drift:
        calls.append(((4, 0), f"{row_link(paths[hub_name], d['id'])} hub/mirror drift: {d['what']}. **Ship or reopen?**"))

    inc, inc_err = None, None
    hook = (args.incident_map.get(cluster) or [None])[0]
    if hook:
        inc, inc_err = read_incidents(hook, args.dry_run or args.no_state)
    open_rows = inc["open"] if inc else []
    hook_decision_ids = {d["id"] for d in (inc["decisions"] if inc else []) if d["id"]}
    # a row already asked about under Your call is not counted again as an incident the agent works
    worked_rows = [o for o in open_rows if not o["needs_you"] and not (o["id"] and o["id"] in hook_decision_ids)]
    for o in open_rows:
        if o["needs_you"]:
            calls.append(((1, 1 if o["action"] == "Close" else 0), decision_row(o)))
    for d in (inc["decisions"] if inc else []):
        ident = link(d["id"], d["url"]) if d["id"] else ""
        calls.append(((2, 0), f"{ident} {bold_question(d['question'])}".strip()))

    # an operator line that opens with the pointing hand is a decision, with the robot a Handled fragment;
    # every other operator line is a Details line
    hand_lines = [f for f in hp["fields"] if f["name"] == "extra" and f["value"].startswith(HAND)]
    robot_lines = [f for f in hp["fields"] if f["name"] == "extra" and f["value"].startswith(ROBOT)]
    for f in hand_lines:
        text = f["value"][len(HAND):].strip()
        due = deadline_of(text, now)
        calls.append(((0, due), text) if due else ((3, 0), text))
    handled_hooks = [t for t in (f["value"][len(ROBOT):].strip() for f in robot_lines) if t]

    # a board past its triage threshold is a card-triage action
    for f in hp["fields"]:
        t = TRIAGE_FAULT_RE.match(f["value"]) if f["name"] == "fault" else None
        if t:
            calls.append(((5, -int(t.group(3))), triage_action(t.group(1), int(t.group(2)), int(t.group(3)), kanban.get(t.group(1)))))

    # a Hermes profile linked to this kit whose skills are out of date: the sweep records
    # the comparison each tick, and a brief with no record compares now
    links = health.get("hermes_links")
    if links is None:
        links = HM.check_links()
    for lk in links:
        if lk.get("stale") and (lk.get("cluster") or args.first_cluster) == cluster:
            calls.append(((6, 0), f"kit skills on `{lk.get('label') or lk.get('profile')}` are stale: re-run `board hermes link`"))
    decisions = [text for _, text in sorted(calls, key=lambda c: c[0])]

    only = cluster in set(args.decisions_only or [])
    feed_faults = ([f"⚠️ incident feed unreadable: {inc_err}"] if inc_err else []) + (inc["faults"] if inc else [])

    # an id in a flapping line becomes a link
    def linkify(line):
        m = re.match(r"^(⚠️ )([A-Z]+-[0-9]+)( flapping between the board and a spoke \()([^)]+)(\))$", line)
        if m and m.group(4) in paths:
            return m.group(1) + row_link(paths[m.group(4)], m.group(2)) + m.group(3) + m.group(4) + m.group(5)
        return line

    attention = [linkify(f["value"]) for f in hp["fields"] if f["name"] == "attention"]
    error_lines = [ln if ln.startswith(("⚠️", "⛔", "❌")) else f"⚠️ {ln}" for ln in attention + feed_faults]
    errors = bool(error_lines)

    # Details day: Monday in Vietnam, or a preview
    weekly = bool(not only and (args.show_boards or datetime.fromtimestamp(now, VN_TZ).weekday() == 0))

    # the one Handled line: hook fragments, incidents the agent works, then sync and bots state
    handled = list(handled_hooks)
    if worked_rows:
        handled.append(f"{len(worked_rows)} incident" + ("" if len(worked_rows) == 1 else "s") + f" with {AGENT}")
    state = []
    if sync_errors:
        state.append(f"❌ sync errors {sync_errors}")
    elif attention:
        state.append(f"⚠️ sync warnings {len(attention)}")
    if inc_err:
        state.append("❌ feed unreadable")
    elif inc and inc["faults"]:
        state.append(f"❌ feed faults {len(inc['faults'])}")
    handled += state or ["sync and bots clean"]

    # the main message: blocks of (name, heading, lines)
    def your_call(shown):
        lines = [f"• {d}" for d in decisions[:shown]]
        if len(decisions) > shown:
            lines.append(f"+{len(decisions) - shown} more")
        return ["decision", f"### 🙋 Your call ({len(decisions)})", lines]

    main = []
    if decisions:
        main.append(your_call(MAX_DECISIONS))
    elif not only and not errors:
        main.append(["clear", "### ✅ Nothing needs you today", []])
    if not only:
        main.append(["handled", "", ["🤖 Handled: " + " · ".join(handled)]])

    # keep the main message under the poster's cap: Your call lines past the first collapse
    def size(blocks):
        return sum(len(h) + 1 + sum(len(x) + 1 for x in ls) + 1 for _, h, ls in blocks)

    shown = min(len(decisions), MAX_DECISIONS)
    while decisions and size(main) > args.main_chars and shown > 1:
        shown -= 1
        main[0] = your_call(shown)

    def render(blocks):
        out = []
        for name, head, ls in blocks:
            if out and name != "handled":
                out.append(("gap", ""))
            if head:
                out.append((f"{name}-head", head))
            out += [(name, x) for x in ls]
        return out

    # Details: the weekly view, or the error lines alone
    detail_lines = list(error_lines)
    if weekly:
        fields_for_boards = [f for f in hp["fields"] if f not in hand_lines and f not in robot_lines]
        detail_lines += board_lines_of(fields_for_boards, kanban, set(args.board_map.get(cluster, [])))
        bot_items = [f"{k} {v}" for k, v in (inc["bots"].items() if inc else []) if v]
        if archived_total:
            bot_items.append(f"archived {archived_total}")
        if bot_items:
            detail_lines.append("🤖 bots: " + ", ".join(bot_items))
        detail_lines += inc["details"] if inc else []
    details = ["### ℹ️ Details"] + detail_lines if detail_lines and not only else []

    fields = [{"name": n, "value": v} for n, v in render(main)]

    day = H.day_stamp(now)
    key = hashlib.sha256(f"brief|{cluster}|{day}".encode()).hexdigest()[:32]
    payload = {
        "kind": "brief", "cluster": cluster, "rail": rail, "key": key,
        "severity": "warn" if decisions or errors else "info",
        "title": f"Daily brief · {cluster}", "date": day, "period_days": 1,
        "next_due": H.day_stamp(now + DAY), "attention": bool(decisions),
        "footer_tail": weekly,
        "fields": fields,
        "data": {"decisions": decisions, "drift": [d["id"] for d in drift], "open_incidents": len(open_rows),
                 "boards_shown": weekly, "archived": archived_total, "sync_errors": sync_errors,
                 "bots": inc["bots"] if inc else {}},
    }
    if details:
        payload["details"] = details
    carried = bstate.get("errors", {}).get(cluster)
    if carried:
        payload["carried_error"] = carried
        payload["fields"].append({"name": "retry", "value": "↻ retry: carried forward after a failed post"})
    return payload, kanban, weekly


# --- run -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

def cmd_run(args):
    now = int(args.now or time.time())
    rows = H.parse_registry(args.registry)
    if not rows:
        print("board brief run: empty or missing --registry", file=sys.stderr)
        return 64
    H.prepare_run_args(args)
    args.incident_map = H.per_cluster_flags(args.incidents)
    args.faults_only = []
    write = not (args.dry_run or args.no_state)
    health = H.read_json(args.health_state_file, {})
    digest = H.read_json(args.state_file, {})
    bstate = health.get("brief", {})

    clusters = H.clusters_of(rows, args.cluster_map)
    args.first_cluster = clusters[0][0] if clusters else ""
    for cluster, rail in clusters:
        if args.cluster and cluster != args.cluster:
            continue
        if not H.is_due(cluster, bstate.get("last_run", {}), args, now):
            nxt = H.day_stamp(bstate["last_run"][cluster] + args.every_days * DAY)
            log(f"skipped(not-due) {cluster} next={nxt}")
            continue
        payload, kanban, boards_shown = compose(cluster, rail, args, rows, health, digest, bstate, now)
        baseline = {s: b["archived_total"] for s, b in kanban.items()}

        def stamp(error=None):
            if not write:
                return
            st = H.read_json(args.health_state_file, {})
            b = st.setdefault("brief", {})
            for k in ("last_run", "archived", "boards_last", "errors"):
                b.setdefault(k, {})
            if error is None:
                b["last_run"][cluster] = now
                if baseline:
                    b["archived"][cluster] = baseline
                if boards_shown:
                    b["boards_last"][cluster] = now
                b["errors"].pop(cluster, None)
            else:
                b["errors"][cluster] = error
            H.write_state(args.health_state_file, st)

        only = cluster in set(args.decisions_only or [])
        if only and not payload["attention"]:
            log(f"skipped(no-decision) {cluster}")
            stamp()
            continue
        line = json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(",", ":"))
        if args.dry_run:
            print(line)
            log(f"{cluster} dry-run (not posted)")
            continue
        if not args.poster:
            print("board brief run: need --poster (or --dry-run)", file=sys.stderr)
            return 64
        try:
            r = subprocess.run(shlex.split(args.poster), input=line, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=180)
            ok, detail = r.returncode == 0, (r.stderr or "").strip()[-400:] or f"poster exit {r.returncode}"
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
            ok, detail = False, str(e)
        if ok:
            stamp()
            log(f"{cluster} posted key={payload['key']}")
        else:
            reason = H.redact(detail, 400)
            stamp(reason)
            log(f"ERROR({reason}) {cluster}")
    return 0


def main(argv=None):
    argv = list(sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv)
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="board brief", description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="mode", required=True)
    p = sub.add_parser("run")
    p.add_argument("--config")
    p.add_argument("--health-state-file", default=H.DEFAULT_HEALTH_STATE)
    p.add_argument("--now", type=int)
    H.add_source_flags(p)
    p.add_argument("--incidents", action="append")
    p.add_argument("--decisions-only", action="append")
    p.add_argument("--every-days", type=float, default=1)
    p.add_argument("--boards-every-days", type=float, default=3)
    p.add_argument("--show-boards", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--main-chars", type=int, default=1250)
    p.add_argument("--poster")
    p.add_argument("--cluster")
    p.add_argument("--force", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--no-state", action="store_true")
    if argv and argv[0] == "run":
        argv = ["run"] + H.expand_config(argv[1:], "brief")
    args = ap.parse_args(argv)
    return cmd_run(args)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
